":8,"pace_html":"<section><h2>Are we on pace today?</h2><div class=\"sub\">Orders so far today against a normal day at the same hour &middot; Pacific</div><div class=\"metrics\"><div class=\"metric hero\"><div class=\"k\">Orders so far</div><div class=\"v\">6</div><span class=\"delta up\">\u25b2 70%</span> vs 3.5 by this hour</div><div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"k\">On track to finish</div><div class=\"v\">16</div>about $3,050</div><div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"k\">A normal full day</div><div class=\"v\">9.6</div>$1,440 in revenue</div></div><div class=\"chartwrap short\"><canvas id=\"pace_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">The red line is today and it stops at the current hour. The dashed line is where a normal day sits at each hour, averaged over the 19 previous days we have. Right now we are <b>ahead of</b> that pace. The finishing figure assumes the rest of today follows the same shape as those days, which off 19 days of history is a rough guide, not a forecast.</p></section>","pace":{"labels":["12a","1a","2a","3a","4a","5a","6a","7a","8a","9a","10a","11a","12p","1p","2p","3p","4p","5p","6p","7p","8p","9p","10p","11p"],"today":[1,1,1,2,2,2,2,4,4,4,6],"avg":[0.11,0.21,0.21,0.37,0.63,0.79,1.11,1.58,2.0,2.89,3.53,4.42,5.26,6.0,6.84,7.37,7.74,8.0,8.21,8.58,9.0,9.42,9.58,9.63],"now_h":10},"traffic_html":"<section><h2>Is traffic still normal?</h2><div class=\"metrics\"><div class=\"metric hero up\"><div class=\"k\">Search clicks, Thu Sep 10</div><div class=\"v\">8,105</div><span class=\"delta up\">+9%</span> vs an average Thursday</div><div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"k\">Analytics engaged visits</div><div class=\"v\">4,442</div><span class=\"delta up\">+18%</span> vs 3,774 average</div><div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"k\">Verdict</div><div class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:19px\"><span class=\"vb flat\">Normal</span></div>Search clicks +9%, still being counted. Analytics +18%.</div></div><div class=\"chartwrap short\"><canvas id=\"traffic_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">Compared against the last 4 Thursdays. US visitors, crawlers excluded, inside 10% is normal. Clicks decide whether traffic moved. When the two lines split apart, Analytics is misreporting, not traffic falling.</p></section>","traffic":{"verdict":"normal","badge":"flat","clicks_final":false,"headline":"Normal","one_line":"Search clicks +9%, still being counted. Analytics +18%.","clicks_cur":8105,"clicks_base":7441,"clicks_pct":8.9,"ga_pct":17.7,"clicks":[5097,5365,7882,8028,8079,7920,7086,5566,5609,8343,7892,8171,7569,6837,5217,5503,7937,8177,7897,7021,6523,4949,5014,5972,8043,8343,8105,590],"verdict_detail":"search clicks and Analytics both inside the usual range","verdict_lines":["Search Console clicks  8,105 vs 7,441 avg Thursday  (+9%)","GA organic engaged     4,442 vs 3,774 avg Thursday  (+18%)","GA sessions w/o source 0.1% of 13,156  (normal 0.1%)"],"base":3774.5,"baseline_days":4,"labels":["8/15","8/16","8/17","8/18","8/19","8/20","8/21","8/22","8/23","8/24","8/25","8/26","8/27","8/28","8/29","8/30","8/31","9/1","9/2","9/3","9/4","9/5","9/6","9/7","9/8","9/9","9/10","9/11"],"organic":[2270,2222,3414,3822,3889,3825,3579,2644,2525,3819,3993,4072,4016,3781,2732,2799,4217,4390,4130,4083,3582,2649,2389,2973,4194,4328,4442,825],"colors":["#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#2f62cc","#fd605b"],"mean":3510,"partial":true},"impact_html":"<section><h2>Did our changes work?</h2><div class=\"sub\">One verdict per change, each measured on the number it should actually move</div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>STD pricing page rebuilt</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 26 &middot; 9:57 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">Our main STD pricing page was rebuilt to Allen's new design, mobile first, with the trust rail carrying the Trustpilot rating and CLIA badge, new copy throughout, and every CTA going straight to the cart.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb good\">Looks better</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on /std-test-pricing/</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Visits that add something to the cart</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 7 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:73%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">8.5%</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 4 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">11.8%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Visits that added something</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 7 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:71%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">26</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 4 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">36</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Organic visits that saw the page</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 7 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">300</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 4 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:93%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">281</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Up 38% on /std-test-pricing/, which clears the 17% that 4 days of traffic can actually resolve. Worth repeating elsewhere. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Place My Order double-click fix</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 21 &middot; 8:30 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">The button stayed live after the first click, so a second click created another Stripe invoice for the same order. Five of the first 19 paid orders went through two or three invoices.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb flat\">No change detected</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on checkout</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Orders needing a second attempt</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0%</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 21 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Orders that retried</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 21 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 21 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">4</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Reads +0% on checkout, inside the 100% that 21 days can resolve, so this is noise rather than a result. It has not made anything worse either.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Checkout stops re-asking for a lab</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 21 &middot; 8:50 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">Checkout showed the whole Test Centers module again even when the shopper had already picked a location, worst on mobile. It now shows the chosen lab with a single Change Location button.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb flat\">No change detected</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on checkout</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders per 100 carts</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0.0%</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 10 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">5.2%</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Paid orders a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:0%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">0</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 10 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">5</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 3 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:98%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">87</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 10 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">88</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Reads +0% on checkout, inside the 29% that 10 days can resolve, so this is noise rather than a result. It has not made anything worse either. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>GEO button to pricing page</b><span class=\"flag funnel\">funnel</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 19 &middot; morning</span></div><p class=\"note\">Clicking Choose This Location on an STD city page now goes to the STD pricing page instead of the city list. Raised and fixed the same day.</p><div class=\"vh\"><span class=\"vb good\">Looks better</span><span class=\"vd\">measured on /std-testing/</span></div><div class=\"cmp\"><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts per 1,000 organic visits</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:52%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">35.2</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 12 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">67.6</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Carts a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:67%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">23</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 12 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">35</span></div></div><div class=\"cmpg\"><div class=\"cmpt\">Organic visits a day</div><div class=\"cmprow\"><label>Before, 1 day</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">653</span></div><div class=\"cmprow after\"><label>Since, 12 days</label><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:77%\"></div></div><span class=\"val\">500</span></div></div></div><p class=\"note\">Up 92% on /std-testing/, which clears the 10% that 12 days of traffic can actually resolve. Visits moved -23%, but 500 is normal for those weekdays (usual 455), so traffic is not the story. Worth repeating elsewhere. 11 days are left out of this because the site recorded no carts on them.</p></div><div class=\"vc\"><div class=\"vh\"><b>Monetization live</b><span class=\"flag launch\">launch</span><span class=\"vd\">Aug 18 &middot; 12:00 AM</span></div><p class=\"note\">Checkout opened on testing.com. First customer order came through at 1:03 AM from Google organic.</p><p class=\"note\">This is the starting line, so there is nothing before it to compare against.</p></div><h3 class=\"mini\">Cart rate since launch</h3><div class=\"chartwrap\"><canvas id=\"chg_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">Carts per 1,000 organic visits, split by the section each change affected, with the whole site dashed for reference. Only changes measured on cart rate appear here. Checkout changes move a different number and are judged on their own cards above, and a change to a page people click through to rather than land on gets its own chart below. A section line is the only place a section-level change can show up: STD GEO is about a tenth of our visits, so a big move there barely dents the sitewide line. Carts are the measure rather than orders because orders run single digits a day and cannot separate signal from noise for weeks. 25 days of data so far.</p><h3 class=\"mini\">Cart rate on /std-test-pricing/</h3><div class=\"chartwrap\"><canvas id=\"chg_page_chart\"></canvas></div><p class=\"note\">Share of organic visits to /std-test-pricing/ that add something to the cart. Counted on the page people <b>viewed</b>, not the page they landed on, which is why this is a separate chart and not another line above. Almost nobody arrives on the pricing page from search, they click through to it, so its landing-page numbers run single digits a day while it fires more than half of every cart on the site. One visit counts once here however many tests it adds, so this is a share of people rather than a count of clicks. The two charts count different groups of people and their heights do not compare.</p><p class=\"note\">Changes are recorded by hand, big ones only, and each needs the right <code>scope</code> and <code>metric</code>. To add one, edit <code>changes.json</code>.</p></section>","impact":{"labels":["Aug 18","Aug 19","Aug 20","Aug 21","Aug 22","Aug 23","Aug 24","Aug 25","Aug 26","Aug 27","Aug 28","Aug 29","Aug 30","Aug 31","Sep 1","Sep 2","Sep 3","Sep 4","Sep 5","Sep 6","Sep 7","Sep 8","Sep 9","Sep 10","Sep 11"],"dates":["2026-08-18","2026-08-19","2026-08-20","2026-08-21","2026-08-22","2026-08-23","2026-08-24","2026-08-2