 against\n    <b>6 real paid orders</b>, and our purchase event sends no order value,\n    so Analytics reports <b>$0 revenue</b> no matter what sells. Use it to see which\n    pages bring people in, never to count orders or money.\n  </div>\n  <h3 class=\"mini\">Traffic and carts by page type</h3>\n  <table class=\"attr\"><thead><tr><th>Page type</th><th>Engaged visits</th><th>Carts</th><th>Cart rate</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr class=\"hot\"><td>/tests/</td><td class=\"amt\">603</td><td class=\"amt\">27</td><td class=\"amt\">4.48%</td></tr><tr class=\"hot\"><td>Homepage</td><td class=\"amt\">312</td><td class=\"amt\">8</td><td class=\"amt\">2.56%</td></tr><tr><td>/treatments/</td><td class=\"amt\">240</td><td class=\"amt\">0</td><td class=\"amt\">0.00%</td></tr><tr class=\"hot\"><td>/std-testing/</td><td class=\"amt\">151</td><td class=\"amt\">19</td><td class=\"amt\">12.58%</td></tr><tr class=\"hot\"><td>Everything else</td><td class=\"amt\">138</td><td class=\"amt\">7</td><td class=\"amt\">5.07%</td></tr><tr><td>/articles/</td><td class=\"amt\">116</td><td class=\"amt\">0</td><td class=\"amt\">0.00%</td></tr><tr class=\"hot\"><td>/blood-testing/</td><td class=\"amt\">13</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td><td class=\"amt\">7.69%</td></tr><tr class=\"hot\"><td>/std-test-pricing</td><td class=\"amt\">5</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td><td class=\"amt\">20.00%</td></tr><tr><td>/find-a-lab</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td><td class=\"amt\">0</td><td class=\"amt\">0.00%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n  <h3 class=\"mini\">By how people arrived</h3>\n  <table class=\"attr\"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Engaged visits</th><th>Carts</th><th>Cart rate</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td>Organic Search</td><td class=\"amt\">825</td><td class=\"amt\">26</td><td class=\"amt\">3.15%</td></tr><tr><td>Direct</td><td class=\"amt\">550</td><td class=\"amt\">22</td><td class=\"amt\">4.00%</td></tr><tr><td>Cross-network</td><td class=\"amt\">186</td><td class=\"amt\">5</td><td class=\"amt\">2.69%</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td class=\"amt\">17</td><td class=\"amt\">0</td><td class=\"amt\">0.00%</td></tr><tr><td>Organic Social</td><td class=\"amt\">3</td><td class=\"amt\">0</td><td class=\"amt\">0.00%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n  <h3 class=\"mini\">By device</h3>\n  <table class=\"attr\"><thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Engaged visits</th><th>Carts</th><th>Cart rate</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody><tr><td>Mobile</td><td class=\"amt\">1,230</td><td class=\"amt\">50</td><td class=\"amt\">4.07%</td></tr><tr><td>Desktop</td><td class=\"amt\">328</td><td class=\"amt\">12</td><td class=\"amt\">3.66%</td></tr><tr><td>Tablet</td><td class=\"amt\">18</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td><td class=\"amt\">5.56%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n  <h3 class=\"mini\">Which page the cart button is actually pressed on</h3><table class=\"attr2\"><thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>Carts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>/std-test-pricing/</td><td class=\"amt\">21</td></tr><tr><td>/tests/complete-blood-count-cbc/</td><td class=\"amt\">18</td></tr><tr><td>/tests/vitamin-a/</td><td class=\"amt\">4</td></tr><tr><td>/</td><td class=\"amt\">3</td></tr><tr><td>/checkout/</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td></tr><tr><td>/std-testing/herpes-1-2-test/</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td></tr><tr><td>/std-testing/standard-std-panel/</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td></tr><tr><td>/tests/</td><td class=\"amt\">1</td></tr></tbody></table>\n  <p class=\"note\"><b>Visits above are engaged sessions</b>, meaning someone actually read\n  the page. Today 2,433 of 4,008 US\n  sessions were non-engaged, almost all of it datacenter crawler traffic from Google Cloud\n  and AWS that loads a page for two seconds and leaves. Counting those would roughly\n  quadruple the denominator and make every rate here look four times worse than reality.</p>\n</section>","notice_html":"<div class=\"notice\"><b>The site stopped recording its checkout events part way through Aug 27, so every cart and checkout figure below is wrong from that day on.</b> Since Aug 28 pu